Ah.  I'm Canadian.  It's a reference to the particle "eh" that we often 
tag onto the ends of questions, and some statements.


An excerpt from my Canadian English Dictionary:
eh (interjection)
1 Used in asking a question or in seeking repetition or confirmation of 
a statement: "It's a nice day, eh?"
2 Used to emphasize a statement or to invite assent or empathy: "It was 
really cold, eh, so we turned on the heater."


It was amusing to me, because many of us really do use this word a 
ridiculous amount.


